###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Speed and memory are measured with ASE on one NVIDIA A6000 (48 GB): NVE MD of 48,000 atoms, 1 fs step, 1 ps (Sec. 3.1); values are figure-only (Figs. 2, 5).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Student, control and teacher force/energy RMSEs versus time per MD step, memory per atom and number of weights, learning curves and RDF errors are figure-only (Figs. 2-5). The text gives only relative statements (more than 2x speed-up at less than half the memory, under 20% force-accuracy loss).
# - The Born Again student is trained on the teacher's atomic energies with the same architecture; the paper contrasts it with knowledge distillation, but the schema's only fitting relation for training on teacher outputs is 'distilled'. The student and control runs each stand for a family of architectures.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/matin2025teacher.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

